diff --git a/README.en.md b/README.en.md
index 17d029f..27c8517 100644
--- a/README.en.md
+++ b/README.en.md
@@ -72,6 +72,22 @@ The build extracts APO3 files from the same pinned restore-tool archive as the
 existing settings. APO3 and APO4 keep separate runtime files and factory
 settings. The control panel uses the same controls; APO3 Clarity maps to Voice.
 
+## ASRock desktop boards Line Out
+
+ASRock boards covered by the official [ASRock Nahimic(v1.10.11\_APO4)](https://download.asrock.com/Utility/Others/Nahimic(v1.10.11_APO4).zip)
+extension driver use its APO4 `Generic_ExternalSpeakers` profile. The vendor
+ships one generic external-speakers tuning for every board in `AVoluteNH3Ext.inf`,
+so all HDA subsystems listed there are matched (`18491897` verified on a
+B650M-H/M.2+ with Realtek ALC897; `18492897`, `18496899`, `18498899` and the
+ALC1220 boards `18492229`–`1849222d` follow the INF). Line Out ports are
+accepted across PipeWire path profiles and UCM naming; plugging in headphones
+bypasses the effects, and HDMI and other outputs keep their normal paths. The
+build extracts the settings from the ASRock installer with `innoextract`, and
+the ASRock factory settings live in `factory-asrock` beside the shared APO4
+vendor runtime. The generic AIstone/MSI restore-tool settings become optional
+at build time, so package builders that cannot reach the Nahimic support site
+can still produce a working desktop build.
+
 ## Contribute device support
 
 Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) first. Include your laptop model, audio hardware IDs, PipeWire output information, and results from testing effect switching, settings persistence, service restarts, and continuous playback. Each model needs a configuration matching its hardware. New device support should be verified on the actual machine before submitting a pull request.
